(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// pyexpat.c: Copyright (c) the Python Software Foundation, under the PSF License Agreement for Python 3.14"] [4 1 "// (LICENSE.md). The port to Go: Copyright (c) the Arbace authors, under the same license."] [6 1 "// The module pyexpat (queue 202e): CPython 3.14.10's Modules/pyexpat.c (with Modules/clinic/pyexpat.c.h's argument"] [7 1 "// parsing and Include/pyexpat.h's PyExpat_CAPI) ported statement for statement over arbace/expat, expat 2.9.0 ported"] [8 1 "// to Go (CPython's vendored Modules/expat). Its C names are kept: the types (xmlparseobject, pyexpat_state,"] [9 1 "// HandlerInfo, ErrorInfo, PyExpat_CAPI), the functions (set_xml_error, conv_string_to_unicode, flag_error,"] [10 1 "// call_with_frame, string_intern, call_character_handler, flush_character_buffer, the my_*Handler trampolines,"] [11 1 "// conv_content_model, get_parse_result, readinst, PyUnknownEncodingHandler, newxmlparseobject, the"] [12 1 "// xmlparse_*_getter/setter, the pyexpat_xmlparser_*_impl methods, add_submodule, add_errors_module,"] [13 1 "// add_model_module, add_features, pyexpat_exec, clear_handlers) and the tables (handler_info, error_info_of,"] [14 1 "// template_buffer)."] [15 1 "//"] [16 1 "// How the C API maps onto pyi's:"] [17 1 "//"] [18 1 "//   - The error indicator. pyexpat.c leans on the thread's error indicator: a handler that fails leaves its"] [19 1 "//     exception set and returns, the next handlers test PyErr_Occurred() and do nothing, and Parse finds the"] [20 1 "//     exception set when XML_Parse returns. pyi raises by returning errors, so the indicator is kept here"] [21 1 "//     (pyexpatErrSet, pyexpatErrOccurred, pyexpatErrFetch), one per thread as CPython's: where C sets an"] [22 1 "//     exception and returns NULL or -1, the Go function sets the indicator and returns nil or -1; where the C"] [23 1 "//     function returns NULL to Python (a method, a getter, a setter), the Go one returns pyexpatErrFetch()."] [24 1 "//   - Reference counting (Py_INCREF, Py_DECREF, Py_XSETREF, Py_CLEAR, PyMem_Free) is Go's collector's, so those"] [25 1 "//     statements are gone; xmlparse_traverse, xmlparse_clear and xmlparse_dealloc have no counterpart (the"] [26 1 "//     XML_Parser is not freed by XML_ParserFree: the collector frees it with the object; the `parent` field"] [27 1 "//     keeps the parent parser alive as CPython's strong reference does, gh-139400)."] [28 1 "//   - The module state. CPython makes the xmlparser type per module object (PyType_FromModuleAndSpec) and finds"] [29 1 "//     the state through the defining class (PyType_GetModuleState(cls)). pyi's built-in types are made once, so"] [30 1 "//     there is one xmlparser type; each parser keeps the state of the module that made it (xmlparseobject.state),"] [31 1 "//     which is what the defining class gives in CPython. The error class and str_read are per module, as CPython's."] [32 1 "//   - Py_BuildValue's \"N\" and \"O&\" conversions fail (return NULL) when one item is NULL: pyexpatBuildValue."] [33 1 "//   - _PyTraceback_Add (call_with_frame): a traceback entry for a frame of a code object with no instructions of"] [34 1 "//     its own, named after the handler, in \"Modules/pyexpat.c\" at the C line of the call, as CPython's"] [35 1 "//     PyCode_NewEmpty frame; pyexpatTracebackAdd."] [36 1 "//   - The methods' docstrings (clinic's PyDoc_STRVAR) are not kept: pyi's built-in methods have no __doc__."] [48 1 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20900: the 64-bit position functions."] [55 1 "// ExpatMemoryHandler is {PyMem_Malloc, PyMem_Realloc, PyMem_Free}: the port ignores the suite's functions (Go's"] [56 1 "// allocator does the work), so its zero value."] [59 1 "// enum HandlerTypes"] [82 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 19504"] [93 1 "// ----------------------------------------------------- //"] [95 1 "// Declarations for objects of type xmlparser"] [99 2 "// Strong reference to a parent `xmlparseobject` if this parser is a child parser. Set to NULL if this parser is"] [100 2 "// a root parser. This is needed to keep the parent parser alive as long as it has at least one child parser."] [101 2 "//"] [102 2 "// See https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/139400 for details."] [104 30 "// Return attributes as a list."] [105 30 "// Report only specified attributes."] [106 30 "// Is a callback active?"] [107 30 "// Namespace-triplets mode?"] [108 30 "// Buffer used when accumulating characters; NULL (nil) if not enabled"] [109 30 "// Size of buffer, in XML_Char units"] [110 30 "// Buffer units in use"] [111 2 "// Whether to defer reparsing of unfinished XML tokens; a de-facto cache of what Expat has the authority on,"] [112 2 "// for lack of a getter API function \"XML_GetReparseDeferralEnabled\" in Expat 2.6.0"] [114 36 "// Dictionary to intern strings (nil: NULL)"] [115 36 "// nil entries are NULL"] [116 2 "// state is the Go-only PyType_GetModuleState(cls): the module that made the parser (see the file's comment)"] [129 1 "// HandlerInfo: C's getset member (a PyGetSetDef per handler, init_handler_descrs') is the type's getset of the"] [130 1 "// handler's name, made in init."] [137 1 "// handler_info is filled in init (its trampolines refer to it, a Go initialization cycle)."] [140 1 "// CALL_XML_HANDLER_SETTER: each HandlerInfo's setter asserts the handler to its expat type (nil: NULL)."] [146 1 "// --- the error indicator (see the file's comment) ---"] [150 1 "// pyexpatErrOccurred is PyErr_Occurred()."] [153 1 "// pyexpatErrSet is PyErr_SetObject and the like: err becomes the thread's pending exception."] [156 1 "// pyexpatErrFetch takes the pending exception, to return it to Python (CPython's return NULL)."] [167 1 "// pyexpatNoMemory is PyErr_NoMemory()."] [170 1 "// pyexpatBuildValue is Py_BuildValue's tuple of \"N\" and \"O&\" items: NULL when one is NULL (its conversion set the"] [171 1 "// error)."] [181 1 "// pyexpatFromUnsigned is PyLong_FromUnsignedLongLong."] [189 1 "// pyexpatAsLong is PyLong_AsLong (-1 with the error set on failure)."] [204 1 "// pyexpatTracebackAdd is _PyTraceback_Add(funcname, filename, lineno): the exception in flight gets an entry for a"] [205 1 "// frame of an empty code object named funcname in filename at lineno (PyCode_NewEmpty), whose globals are a new"] [206 1 "// dict, as the frame the C code runs in."] [223 1 "// pyexpatStrlen is strlen of a C string."] [226 1 "// pyexpatAsUTF8 is PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize as a C string (NUL-terminated); the error is returned."] [231 1 "// pyexpatStrArg is clinic's str converter (accept={str} or {str, NoneType}): a C string, NULL for None when"] [232 1 "// acceptNone; the embedded NUL and the bad argument errors as clinic's."] [255 1 "// pyexpatBadArgument is _PyArg_BadArgument."] [264 1 "// pyexpatPosOnly is _PyArg_UnpackKeywords for clinic's positional-only parameters (minpos to maxpos of them)."] [287 1 "// pyexpatArgO is METH_O's check: the one argument. funcstr is _PyObject_FunctionStr's name (\"xmlparser.SetBase\","] [288 1 "// \"pyexpat.ErrorString\")."] [299 1 "// pyexpatNoArgs is METH_NOARGS' check (funcstr as pyexpatArgO's)."] [319 1 "// Set an integer attribute on the error object; return true on success, false on an exception."] [329 1 "// set_xml_error: errmsg \"\" stands for C's NULL (no caller passes an empty message)."] [359 1 "// SET_XML_ERROR"] [374 1 "// Build and set an Expat exception, including positioning information. Always returns NULL."] [390 1 "// Convert a string of XML_Chars into a Unicode string. Returns None if str is a null pointer."] [392 2 "// XXX currently this code assumes that XML_Char is 8-bit, and hence in UTF-8."] [393 2 "// UTF-8 from Expat, Unicode desired"] [410 2 "// XXX currently this code assumes that XML_Char is 8-bit, and hence in UTF-8."] [411 2 "// UTF-8 from Expat, Unicode desired"] [423 1 "// Callback routines"] [425 1 "// This handler is used when an error has been detected, in the hope that actual parsing can be terminated"] [426 1 "// early. This will only help if an external entity reference is encountered."] [431 1 "// Dummy character data handler used when an error (exception) has been detected, and the actual parsing can be"] [432 1 "// terminated early. This is needed since character data handler can't be safely removed from within the"] [433 1 "// character data handler, but can be replaced. It is used only from the character data handler trampoline, and"] [434 1 "// must be used right after `flag_error()` is called."] [436 2 "// Do nothing."] [444 1 "// call_with_frame: lineno is the C line of the call in pyexpat.c (__LINE__; for the RC_HANDLER macro's handlers,"] [445 1 "// the line of the macro's invocation)."] [460 2 "// result can be NULL if the unicode conversion failed."] [479 2 "// assert((value != NULL) == !PyErr_Occurred()): not kept, as release builds compile it out (a Py_BuildValue's"] [480 2 "// later item interned after an earlier one failed has value set and the error set)"] [484 1 "// Return 0 on success, -1 on exception. flag_error() will be called before return if needed."] [493 2 "// Copy the buffer before tuple allocation can trigger a GC callback."] [501 2 "// temp is now a borrowed reference; consider it unused."] [507 2 "// temp is an owned reference again, or NULL"] [522 2 "// The callback may change buffering or install a new handler, which also flushes. Do not expose the same"] [523 2 "// pending data a second time."] [540 3 "// The callback may replace the handler or disable buffering."] [569 3 "// Set max to the number of slots filled in atts[]; max/2 is the number of attributes we need to process."] [578 3 "// Build the container."] [579 3 "// Intern-dictionary comparisons can change the mode mid-loop."] [581 21 "// the list's items (PyList_New(max))"] [623 3 "// Container is now a borrowed reference; ignore it."] [637 1 "// RC_HANDLER is the macro's body, shared by the trampolines it defines (VOID_HANDLER, INT_HANDLER and"] [638 1 "// ExternalEntityRef's): NAME the handler's index, funcname its #NAME, lineno the invocation's line; build is"] [639 1 "// PARSE_FORMAT's Py_BuildValue (nil when a conversion failed). It returns the handler's result (rv), nil when no"] [640 1 "// handler was called or it raised; CONVERSION is the caller's."] [723 50 "// PyTuple_New(model->numchildren)"] [747 2 "// C's locals of the if block, hoisted: Go's goto may not jump over their declarations"] [799 1 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 19504"] [861 1 "// #define my_DefaultHandlerExpand my_DefaultHandlerExpandHandler"] [864 1 "// INT_HANDLER(NotStandalone): rc = PyLong_AsLong(rv), the C int."] [888 1 "// XXX UnknownEncodingHandler"] [904 1 "// check that the current function is not called from within a handler"] [912 1 "// ----------------------------------------------------------------"] [930 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.SetReparseDeferralEnabled(enabled: bool, /)"] [932 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20600"] [942 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.GetReparseDeferralEnabled()"] [947 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.Parse(data, isfinal=False, /)"] [948 1 "//"] [949 1 "// Parse XML data. 'data' can be a bytes-like object or a string. If it is a string, the encoding declaration in"] [950 1 "// the XML data is ignored. 'isfinal' should be true at end of input."] [952 2 "// avoid re-entrant calls to XML_Parse()"] [959 14 "// C's s advancing: the offset into s"] [969 3 "// Explicitly set UTF-8 encoding. Return code ignored."] [979 16 "// a C buffer is never NULL"] [998 1 "// File reading copied from cPickle"] [1027 2 "// len <= buf_size <= INT_MAX"] [1031 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.ParseFile(file, /)"] [1032 1 "//"] [1033 1 "// Parse XML data from a binary file-like object. Its read() method should return bytes."] [1035 2 "// avoid re-entrant calls to XML_GetBuffer() or XML_ParseBuffer()"] [1077 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.SetBase(base: str, /): Set the base URL for the parser."] [1086 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.GetBase(): Return base URL string for the parser."] [1095 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.GetInputContext(): Return the input which generated the current event as bytes."] [1096 1 "//"] [1097 1 "// The data is in the encoding of the entity which contains the text. It extends to the end of the currently"] [1098 1 "// buffered input, therefore it can contain also the data of the following events, and if the event was generated"] [1099 1 "// by a large amount of text, not all of it may be available."] [1102 3 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20900"] [1117 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.ExternalEntityParserCreate(context: str(accept={str, NoneType}), encoding: str = NULL, /)"] [1118 1 "//"] [1119 1 "// Create a parser for parsing an external entity based on the information passed to the ExternalEntityRefHandler."] [1135 2 "// The new subparser will make use of the parent XML_Parser inside of Expat. So we need to take subparsers into"] [1136 2 "// account with the reference counting of their parent parser."] [1151 2 "// allocate and clear handlers first"] [1154 3 "// do nothing"] [1160 2 "// then copy handlers from self"] [1173 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.SetParamEntityParsing(flag: int, /)"] [1174 1 "//"] [1175 1 "// Controls parsing of parameter entities (including the external DTD subset). Possible flag values are"] [1176 1 "// XML_PARAM_ENTITY_PARSING_NEVER, XML_PARAM_ENTITY_PARSING_UNLESS_STANDALONE and XML_PARAM_ENTITY_PARSING_ALWAYS."] [1177 1 "// Returns true if setting the flag was successful."] [1183 1 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 19505"] [1184 1 "//"] [1185 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.UseForeignDTD(flag: bool = True, /)"] [1186 1 "//"] [1187 1 "// Allows the application to provide an artificial external subset if one is not specified as part of the"] [1188 1 "// document instance. This readily allows the use of a 'default' document type controlled by the application,"] [1189 1 "// while still getting the advantage of providing document type information to the parser. 'flag' defaults to"] [1190 1 "// True if not provided."] [1207 1 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20400"] [1213 2 "// The setter fails if self->itself is NULL (which is not possible here) or is a non-root parser, which"] [1214 2 "// currently only happens for parsers created by ExternalEntityParserCreate()."] [1225 2 "// The setter fails if self->itself is NULL (which is not possible here), is a non-root parser, which currently"] [1226 2 "// only happens for parsers created by ExternalEntityParserCreate(), or if 'max_factor' is NaN or < 1.0."] [1228 2 "// Note: Expat has no API to determine whether a parser is a root parser, and since the Expat functions for"] [1229 2 "// defining the various maximum allowed amplifcation factors fail when a bad parser or an out-of-range factor"] [1230 2 "// is given without specifying which check failed, we check whether the factor is out-of-range to improve the"] [1231 2 "// error message. See also gh-90949."] [1240 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.SetBillionLaughsAttackProtectionActivationThreshold(threshold: unsigned_long_long, /)"] [1245 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.SetBillionLaughsAttackProtectionMaximumAmplification(max_factor: float, /)"] [1250 1 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20702"] [1251 1 "//"] [1252 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.SetAllocTrackerActivationThreshold(threshold: unsigned_long_long, /)"] [1257 1 "// pyexpat.xmlparser.SetAllocTrackerMaximumAmplification(max_factor: float, /)"] [1262 1 "// ---------- //"] [1264 1 "// pyexpat international encoding support. Make it as simple as possible."] [1295 21 "// Py_UNICODE_REPLACEMENT_CHARACTER"] [1309 1 "// pyexpatHashSalt16 is _Py_HashSecret.expat.hashsalt16: the secret's first 16 bytes, which its union shares with"] [1310 1 "// siphash's k0 and k1 (pyi's HashKey)."] [1333 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20600"] [1336 2 "// namespace_separator is either NULL or contains one char + \\0"] [1343 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20800: This feature was added upstream in libexpat 2.8.0."] [1349 3 "// do nothing"] [1371 3 "// If we're changing the character data handler, flush all cached data with the old handler. Not sure"] [1372 3 "// there's a \"right\" thing to do, though, but this probably won't happen."] [1380 3 "// If this is the character data handler, and a character data handler is already active, we need to be"] [1381 3 "// more careful. What we can safely do is replace the existing character data handler callback function"] [1382 3 "// with a no-op function that will refuse to call Python. The downside is that this doesn't completely"] [1383 3 "// remove the character data handler from the C layer if there's any callback active, so Expat does a"] [1384 3 "// little more work than it otherwise would, but that's really an odd case. A more elaborate system of"] [1385 3 "// handlers and state could remove the C handler more effectively."] [1398 1 "// INT_GETTER(name, func)"] [1453 2 "// trivial case -- no change"] [1458 2 "// check maximum"] [1464 3 "// there is already a buffer"] [1470 3 "// free existing buffer"] [1538 1 "// End of code for xmlparser objects"] [1539 1 "// --------------------------------------------------------"] [1541 1 "// pyexpat.ParserCreate(encoding: str(accept={str, NoneType}) = None, namespace_separator: str(accept={str,"] [1542 1 "// NoneType}) = None, intern: object = NULL): Return a new XML parser object."] [1550 2 "// Explicitly passing None means no interning is desired. Not passing anything means that a new dictionary is"] [1551 2 "// used."] [1567 1 "// pyexpat.ErrorString(code: long, /): Returns string error for given number."] [1576 1 "// Module docstring"] [1579 1 "// Initialization function for the module"] [1583 1 "// init_handler_descrs is done once, in init, on the one xmlparser type (see the file's comment)."] [1596 1 "// PyModule_New(fullname)'s dictionary."] [1619 2 "// gives away the reference to the submodule"] [1626 21 "// Error constant name, e.g. \"XML_ERROR_NO_MEMORY\""] [1627 21 "// Error description as returned by XML_ErrorString(<int>)"] [1631 12 "// XML_ERROR_NONE (value 0) is not exposed"] [1660 2 "// Added in Expat 1.95.7."] [1663 2 "// Added in Expat 1.95.8."] [1675 2 "// Added in 2.0.0."] [1680 2 "// Added in 2.2.1."] [1683 2 "// Added in 2.3.0."] [1686 2 "// Added in 2.4.0."] [1689 2 "// Added in 2.6.4."] [1693 1 "// pyexpatFromString is PyUnicode_FromString (UTF-8, strict)."] [1702 2 "// NOTE: This keeps the source of truth regarding error messages with libexpat and (by definition) in"] [1703 2 "// bulletproof sync with the other uses of the XML_ErrorString function elsewhere within this file. pyexpat's"] [1704 2 "// copy of the messages only acts as a fallback in case of outdated runtime libexpat, where it returns NULL."] [1705 2 "//"] [1706 2 "// In addition, XML_ErrorString is assumed to return UTF-8 encoded strings (in conv_string_to_unicode, we"] [1707 2 "// decode them using 'strict' error handling)."] [1720 39 "// PyModule_AddStringConstant"] [1724 51 "// PyDict_SetItemString"] [1791 1 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION > 19505"] [1797 3 "// Py_BuildValue(\"si\", ...): the name decoded, the value a C int"] [1808 1 "// Include/pyexpat.h: stuff to export relevant 'expat' entry points from pyexpat to other parser modules, such as"] [1809 1 "// cElementTree."] [1815 1 "// PyExpat_CAPI is struct PyExpat_CAPI: its fields in C's order, the function pointers as Go funcs of the expat"] [1816 1 "// port's signatures."] [1817 1 "//"] [1818 1 "// What _elementtree (Modules/_elementtree.c, not ported) takes from it, for its later port: it reads the capsule"] [1819 1 "// pyexpat.expat_CAPI (PyCapsule_Import, here the capsule's pointer field), checks magic == PyExpat_CAPI_MAGIC,"] [1820 1 "// size >= sizeof(struct PyExpat_CAPI) and MAJOR/MINOR/MICRO_VERSION equal to its own expat.h's, then calls through"] [1821 1 "// it (its EXPAT(st, func) macro): ParserCreate_MM, ParserFree, SetUserData, SetElementHandler,"] [1822 1 "// SetCharacterDataHandler, SetCommentHandler, SetProcessingInstructionHandler, SetDefaultHandlerExpand,"] [1823 1 "// SetNamespaceDeclHandler, SetStartDoctypeDeclHandler, SetUnknownEncodingHandler with"] [1824 1 "// DefaultUnknownEncodingHandler, SetEncoding, SetHashSalt16Bytes (else SetHashSalt), SetReparseDeferralEnabled,"] [1825 1 "// Parse, GetErrorCode, GetErrorLineNumber, GetErrorColumnNumber and ErrorString. Its handlers raise into the same"] [1826 1 "// error indicator (pyexpatErrSet; its parse checks pyexpatErrOccurred as _elementtree checks PyErr_Occurred) and"] [1827 1 "// DefaultUnknownEncodingHandler is PyUnknownEncodingHandler, which sets it."] [1829 23 "// set to PyExpat_CAPI_MAGIC"] [1830 23 "// set to sizeof(struct PyExpat_CAPI)"] [1834 2 "// pointers to selected expat functions. add new functions at the end, if needed"] [1853 2 "// might be NULL for expat < 2.1.0"] [1855 2 "// might be NULL for expat < 2.6.0"] [1857 2 "// might be NULL for expat < 2.7.2"] [1860 2 "// might be NULL for expat < 2.4.0"] [1863 2 "// might be NULL for expat < 2.8.0"] [1865 2 "// always add new stuff to the end!"] [1868 1 "// sizeof_PyExpat_CAPI is sizeof(struct PyExpat_CAPI) on LP64: the magic pointer (8), the size and the three versions"] [1869 1 "// (4 each), then 25 function pointers (8 each): 8 + 16 + 200."] [1876 2 "// init_handler_descrs(state) ran in init."] [1878 55 "// PyErr_NewException(\"xml.parsers.expat.ExpatError\", NULL, NULL)"] [1886 2 "// Add some symbolic constants to the module"] [1904 2 "// XXX When Expat supports some way of figuring out how it was compiled, this should check and set"] [1905 2 "// native_encoding appropriately."] [1916 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION > 19505"] [1930 2 "// initialize pyexpat dispatch table"] [1954 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20100"] [1956 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20800"] [1958 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20600"] [1960 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20702"] [1963 2 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 20400"] [1967 2 "// export using capsule (pyexpat_capsule_destructor's PyMem_Free is the collector's)"] [1989 1 "// pyexpatSelf is the method descriptor's check of its first argument."] [2001 1 "// pyexpatULongLong is clinic's unsigned_long_long converter (_PyLong_UnsignedLongLong_Converter)."] [2017 1 "// pyexpatFloat is clinic's float converter: (float)PyFloat_AsDouble."] [2019 31 "// PyFloat_CheckExact"] [2029 1 "// xmlparse_methods and the getsets (the clinic wrappers' argument parsing, then the _impl)."] [2035 2 "// Py_TPFLAGS_DISALLOW_INSTANTIATION"] [2185 2 "// xmlparse_members: intern, read-only (_Py_T_OBJECT: NULL reads as None)"] [2192 58 "// a Py_READONLY member's"] [2195 2 "// xmlparse_getsetlist"] [2219 2 "// HANDLER_INFO(name): {#name, XML_Set##name, my_##name}; each setter asserts the handler to its expat type"] [2220 2 "// (C's cast to xmlhandlersetter), a nil handler setting NULL."] [2306 3 "// XML_COMBINED_VERSION >= 19504"] [2325 3 "// pyexpat_methods"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[215 25] [312 41] [322 39] [350 29] [470 38] [588 12] [588 21] [603 35] [727 11] [727 41] [736 52] [868 101] [882 4] [953 47] [963 27] [1036 51] [1153 11] [1153 34] [1161 12] [1161 35] [1293 11] [1293 20] [1348 11] [1348 34] [1441 22] [1556 35] [1585 12] [1585 35] [1614 47] [1724 36] [1729 40] [1746 22] [1746 56] [1796 12] [1796 60] [1979 12] [1979 35] [2019 24] [2083 57] [2089 65] [2105 93] [2179 75] [2187 38] [2333 88] [2338 110]] :go/trails [[1690 49] [2310 62]]} (go/file "builtins_pyexpat.go" :imports [

    ;; pyexpat.c: Copyright (c) the Python Software Foundation, under the PSF License Agreement for Python 3.14
    ;; (LICENSE.md). The port to Go: Copyright (c) the Arbace authors, under the same license.

    ;; The module pyexpat (queue 202e): CPython 3.14.10's Modules/pyexpat.c (with Modules/clinic/pyexpat.c.h's argument
    ;; parsing and Include/pyexpat.h's PyExpat_CAPI) ported statement for statement over arbace/expat, expat 2.9.0 ported
    ;; to Go (CPython's vendored Modules/expat). Its C names are kept: the types (xmlparseobject, pyexpat_state,
    ;; HandlerInfo, ErrorInfo, PyExpat_CAPI), the functions (set_xml_error, conv_string_to_unicode, flag_error,
    ;; call_with_frame, string_intern, call_character_handler, flush_character_buffer, the my_*Handler trampolines,
    ;; conv_content_model, get_parse_result, readinst, PyUnknownEncodingHandler, newxmlparseobject, the
    ;; xmlparse_*_getter/setter, the pyexpat_xmlparser_*_impl methods, add_submodule, add_errors_module,
    ;; add_model_module, add_features, pyexpat_exec, clear_handlers) and the tables (handler_info, error_info_of,
    ;; template_buffer).
    ;;
    ;; How the C API maps onto pyi's:
    ;;
    ;;   - The error indicator. pyexpat.c leans on the thread's error indicator: a handler that fails leaves its
    ;;     exception set and returns, the next handlers test PyErr_Occurred() and do nothing, and Parse finds the
    ;;     exception set when XML_Parse returns. pyi raises by returning errors, so the indicator is kept here
    ;;     (pyexpatErrSet, pyexpatErrOccurred, pyexpatErrFetch), one per thread as CPython's: where C sets an
    ;;     exception and returns NULL or -1, the Go function sets the indicator and returns nil or -1; where the C
    ;;     function returns NULL to Python (a method, a getter, a setter), the Go one returns pyexpatErrFetch().
    ;;   - Reference counting (Py_INCREF, Py_DECREF, Py_XSETREF, Py_CLEAR, PyMem_Free) is Go's collector's, so those
    ;;     statements are gone; xmlparse_traverse, xmlparse_clear and xmlparse_dealloc have no counterpart (the
    ;;     XML_Parser is not freed by XML_ParserFree: the collector frees it with the object; the `parent` field
    ;;     keeps the parent parser alive as CPython's strong reference does, gh-139400).
    ;;   - The module state. CPython makes the xmlparser type per module object (PyType_FromModuleAndSpec) and finds
    ;;     the state through the defining class (PyType_GetModuleState(cls)). pyi's built-in types are made once, so
    ;;     there is one xmlparser type; each parser keeps the state of the module that made it (xmlparseobject.state),
    ;;     which is what the defining class gives in CPython. The error class and str_read are per module, as CPython's.
    ;;   - Py_BuildValue's "N" and "O&" conversions fail (return NULL) when one item is NULL: pyexpatBuildValue.
    ;;   - _PyTraceback_Add (call_with_frame): a traceback entry for a frame of a code object with no instructions of
    ;;     its own, named after the handler, in "Modules/pyexpat.c" at the C line of the call, as CPython's
